<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bangkok</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Krung Thep</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bangkok is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a>, on the Chao Phraya river near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gulf-of-thailand">Gulf of Thailand</a>. King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rama-i">Rama I</a> founded it as the capital of the Chakri dynasty in 1782 on Rattanakosin island, opposite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taksin">Taksin</a>'s capital at Thonburi, and laid it out on the model of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayutthaya-kingdom">Ayutthaya</a>. It became the political, religious and commercial centre of Siam and the seat of modern Thailand's government.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bangkok.jpg" alt="Bangkok" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ninara from Helsinki, Finland · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:4Y1A1159_Bangkok_(33536795515).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
